        {
          "id": 2154943902,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Faking it, in that it's an IANA registered port, but when over TCP it could be\n1) NVMe/TCP PDU directly \n2) TLS record containing NVMe/TCP (reject, TLS heuristic dissector is strong and will find it)\n3) The middle of a PDU split across segments, if the capture started in the middle (reject and wait until we get a PDU start, because tcp_dissect_pdus will break.)\n\nThis runs a quick test at the start of a connection to make sure that it's the start of a PDU.\n\nWe have a more general need in multiplexing cases for a way to say \"not my protocol, but I know what it is\" that removes the current protocol (e.g. in RTP/STUN/DTLS/QUIC), but this works because the TLS heuristic is strong.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
