      "title": "NVMe/TCP: Distinguish between over TCP and over TLS",
      "message": "NVMe/TCP: Distinguish between over TCP and over TLS\n\nNVMe/TCP allows PDUs to span TCP segments (see Figure 5 of the NVMe/TCP\nTransport Specification.) Also, some connections are over TLS.\nLuckily, the PDU types for NVMe/TCP occupy the first byte, same as\nthe Content Type for TLS Records, and while these PDU types go to 11,\nTLS Content Types start at 20 (and won't change, to enable multiplexing,\nsee RFC 9443.)\n\nAlso add the two new PDU types to the enum and value string (not\ndissected yet) and fix the location of the flags bitmask.\n\nPing #20123\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-10-10T21:59:01.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
